{"resourceIdentifier":"4456","resourceName":"CREATING LIVELIHOOD OPPORTUNITIES AND CARBON CREDIT INCOME FOR SMALLHOLDER FARMERS THROUGH HORTICULTURAL PLANTATIONS IN BANGLADESH","description":"Agroforestry is a land use management system combining trees with crops or livestock on the same land. Agroforestry is widely practiced in Bangladesh, particularly in rural areas where it is an important component of smallholder farming systems. It is used for food production and environmental services. The project is located in Bangladesh and Chapainawabganj, Nogaon, and Rajshahi districts of Bangladesh are considered in the first instance. As we move forward, the benefits of horticulture-based agroforestry ecosystems will also be brought to other parts of the country. The country is home to many fauna and flora and has five different types of ecosystem i.e., coastal ecosystem, inland freshwater ecosystem, terrestrial forest ecosystem, and hilly ecosystem. The main aim of the project activity includes the plantation of fruit-bearing trees on the farmlands of smallholder farmers. The agroforestry systems deliver several forest products, agriculture products, and ecosystem services which may enhance the social well-being of the local farmers and national and global community. The primary activity of the project is to onboard farmers who are practicing agroforestry plantations on their farmland. The Project Proponent along with the local implementation partner will implement project activity including plantation activities, along with capacity building and training programs. The species selected for agroforestry plantation include Mango and Guava but will be diversified further over time. The implementation of the project would generate GHG emission removals and improve the local environment through growth of the trees, increasing the source of income, and enhancing the capabilities of farmers. The project is expected to generate annual average GHG emission reductions or removals of 167,587 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":23.777176,"longitude":90.399452},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-11-22","endExclusive":"2023-12-23","endInclusive":"2023-12-22"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4456"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Varaha ClimateAg Private Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"Delhi, India"},{"type":"string","value":"+91-9619776814"},{"type":"string","value":"madhur.jain@varahaag.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4456"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4456"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"567407"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":23983}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5000 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Carbon Check (India) Private Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"29/04/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 15/06/2020 - 14/06/2040"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=93691&IDKEY=ulksjoiuwqowrnoiuomnckjashoufifmln902309ksdflku098s129199889","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"PROJ_DESC_DRAFT_4456_30MAY2023.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-07-10T19:07:49.967Z"},{"uri":